# DevFlow Core v2

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md) as the shared project rule source.

Use `Sense -> Brainstorm -> Cut -> Shape -> Build -> Prove` as the default lightweight development flow.

Authoritative method source: `skills/devflow-core/references/core-methods.md`.

Rules:

- For normal development work, load `devflow-core` when CodeBuddy supports skills. If skills are unavailable, follow this rule file.
- If the user asks to implement, fix, build, or land something, do not stop at Shape; continue through Build and Prove.
- If the user reports a problem without explicitly asking for a fix, prove the facts first and re-route only after the needed change is known.
- If the user challenges the result, says changed wrong, says your code is wrong/you wrote it wrong/has a problem/not right/missing/incomplete/still missing/有问题/不对/写错了/少了/少个/缺少/缺漏/遗漏/漏了, reports a quality complaint, or repeated edits miss, run `devflow-pua`: stop the current approach, read local methodology-router/methodology-library/flavor-display references, quarantine old wrong context, classify User-view miss and Satisfaction gap, show `METHOD: {flavor} / {method}`, restart `devflow-brainstorm`, ask what is wrong and what result is wanted when not inferable, switch to a different/opposite method when the prior method failed, then prove.
- For any requirement, behavior change, feature, architecture change, or ambiguous ask, run Brainstorm and Cut before Build unless Design-lite is justified by clear behavior, one plausible path, low risk, local impact, and quick proof.
- If a request might be Fast, Design-lite, or full Design and facts do not decide it, ask the user to choose the route instead of guessing.
- Before writing new code, run the Ponytail Ladder: no change, reuse existing code, standard library, native platform, installed dependency, one-line/config, minimum new code.
- For bug fixes, search callers/references before editing and choose shared vs narrow fix intentionally.
- Mark deliberate simplifications with `devflow: <ceiling>, revisit when <trigger>` so `/devflow-debt` can harvest them.
- Apply Karpathy Minimal Change: touch only the files needed for the user goal; do not add speculative abstraction or opportunistic refactors.
- Before adding a dependency, abstraction, config, directory, framework layer, or generic engine, explain why it is needed now.
- Before reporting done, run verification and output command, result, and `PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED`.
- Build is blocked until `Reuse Check`, `Overbuild Check`, `Diff Check`, and `Scope Check` are answered.

Design output:

```text
Goal:
Smallest useful plan:
Not doing:
Impact:
Verification:
```

Completion proof:

```text
Command:
Result:
Judgment: PASS / FAIL / BLOCKED
```
